  "kind": "definition",
  "fullName": "Int.sqrt",
  "endPos": 866,
  "detail":
  "```lean\nInt.sqrt (z : ℤ) : ℤ\n```\n***\n`sqrt z` is the square root of an integer `z`. If `z` is positive, it returns the largest\ninteger `r` such that `r * r ≤ n`. If it is negative, it returns `0`. For example, `sqrt (-1) = 0`,\n`sqrt 1 = 1`, `sqrt 2 = 1` ",
  "definitionStartPos": {"line": 26, "column": 4},
  "definitionPath":
  "/Users/hattoriseiji/Autoinformalization/ExportInfos/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Data/Int/Sqrt.lean",
  "definitionEndPos": {"line": 26, "column": 8}},
